NAME
    find - search for files by name under the CWD

SYNOPSIS
    find pattern

DESCRIPTION
    Walks the current directory tree depth-first and prints the full path
    of every entry (file or directory) whose name matches. If the pattern
    contains * or ? it is a case-insensitive glob; otherwise it is a
    literal substring match. Searches the CWD subtree only. find is a
    /bin program.

LIMITS
    Descends at most 10 levels below the CWD, and records at most 24
    subdirectories per level. Anything deeper or wider is skipped
    silently -- find prints what it found, with no warning that part of
    the tree went unsearched.

EXAMPLES
    find .TXT            names containing ".TXT"
    find *.c             names matching a glob
    find TEST?.ASM       glob with a single-char wildcard

SEE ALSO
    dir, tree, grep
